<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Etruscan League</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 264 BCE (approx.) · capital Volsinii</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Federation of twelve Etruscan city-states that met yearly at the sanctuary of Voltumna, more a religious union than a military alliance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>By the 6th century BCE the leading cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a> formed a group known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as the twelve peoples of Etruria. Its focus was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fanum-voltumnae">Fanum Voltumnae</a>, a federal sanctuary near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volsinii">Volsinii</a>, possibly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campo-della-fiera">Campo della Fiera</a> below <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-orvieto">Orvieto</a>, where delegates met each spring.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The list of members changed over time but usually included <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veii">Veii</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caere">Caere</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tarquinii">Tarquinii</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vulci">Vulci</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volsinii">Volsinii</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/clusium">Clusium</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/perusia">Perusia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cortona">Cortona</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arretium">Arretium</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volaterrae">Volaterrae</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vetulonia">Vetulonia</a> or <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rusellae">Rusellae</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/populonia">Populonia</a>. The annual gathering combined sacrifices, games and markets with political councils, and chose a federal leader whose powers were mainly ceremonial. It rarely acted together in war: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> says it refused to help Veii against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> conquered the Etruscan cities one by one, the League lost all political weight, ending with the destruction of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volsinii">Volsinii</a> in 264 BCE. Under the Empire a ceremonial league of fifteen peoples was revived with a praetor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a>, and the festival was still held in the 4th century CE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/etruscan-league.jpg" alt="Etruscan League" width="320" height="389"><figcaption>Image: NormanEinstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etruscan_civilization_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 264 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Volsinii</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Etruscan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Etruscan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Etruscan Dodecapolis, Twelve Cities of Etruria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-432&amp;focus=etruscan-league" aria-label="Etruscan League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4970 662 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Etruscan League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5290 918L5304 942M5290 918L5301 938M5290 918L5285 931M5290 918L5294 938M5290 918L5282 925M5290 918L5290 918M5290 918L5288 906M5290 918L5299 903M5290 918L5286 892M5290 918L5262 894M5290 918L5265 911M5290 918L5270 912M5290 918L5253 907M5290 918L5289 898"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5301 938h0M5285 931h0M5294 938h0M5282 925h0M5290 918h0M5288 906h0M5299 903h0M5286 892h0M5262 894h0